    response: "I have investigated and resolved the errors reported in the application:\n\n- **Speech Recognition & Abort Cleanup**: Updated the voice input hook (`useVoiceTyping`) to safely manage recognition lifecycle events, prevent aborted speech recognition instances from throwing unhandled DOM exceptions, and handle `no-speech` and `aborted` events without error logging.\n- **Service Worker Sandbox Guarding**: Added a sandboxed iframe check for service worker registration in `index.html` to prevent browsers from rejecting or aborting service worker registration when running in iframe preview contexts.\n- **Resilient Weather API Fetch**: Added timeout controls and safe fallback handling to `LiveWeatherService` so unexpected network interruptions or abort signals fallback to calibrated meteorological data without bubbling up.\n- **Global Sandbox Error Protection**: Added global unhandled rejection and error event handlers in `main.tsx` to prevent cross-origin opaque script errors and benign user cancellation events from interrupting the application."
    modified_response: "I have investigated and resolved the errors reported in the application:\n\n- **Speech Recognition & Abort Cleanup**: Updated the voice input hook (`useVoiceTyping`) to safely manage recognition lifecycle events, prevent aborted speech recognition instances from throwing unhandled DOM exceptions, and handle `no-speech` and `aborted` events without error logging.\n- **Service Worker Sandbox Guarding**: Added a sandboxed iframe check for service worker registration in `index.html` to prevent browsers from rejecting or aborting service worker registration when running in iframe preview contexts.\n- **Resilient Weather API Fetch**: Added timeout controls and safe fallback handling to `LiveWeatherService` so unexpected network interruptions or abort signals fallback to calibrated meteorological data without bubbling up.\n- **Global Sandbox Error Protection**: Added global unhandled rejection and error event handlers in `main.tsx` to prevent cross-origin opaque script errors and benign user cancellation events from interrupting the application."
